     </tr>
     <tr style="height:12pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;text-indent:14.4pt;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="margin-left:14.4pt;text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:12pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Sales by region</font></p><p style="text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Our global organic sales* decreased by 1.1% compared to the global LVP decrease of 1.9% (according to Mobility Global, Oct 2026). The relative outperformance was positively impacted by product launches but negatively impacted by regional and model LVP mix development (around 90 bps). Our organic sales growth* outperformed LVP growth by 2.5pp in Asia excluding China and by 1.1pp in China. We underperformed LVP in EMEA by 3.7pp. Performance in the Americas overall was in line with LVP, while North America delivered stronger results, outperforming LVP by close to 2 percentage points.</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">LVP in China declined by 6.9%, with Global OEMs LVP declining by 25% and Chinese OEMs LVP growing by 1.4%. Autoliv's sales to domestic OEMs increased organically by around 21% while our sales to global OEMs decreased by around 29%. Chinese OEMs accounted for 58% of our sales in China in the quarter, compared to around 46% a year ago. We expect continued strong 2026 sales performance with domestic OEMs. Our strong sales growth in Asia excluding China was mainly due to 29% organic sales growth in India, reflecting strong LVP growth and the trend of increased safety content in vehicles in India.</font></p></td>
     </tr>
