     <tr style="height:12pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:12pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Sales by product &#x2013; Airbags, Steering Wheels and Other</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Sales for Airbags, Steering Wheels and Other grew organically* by 1.3% in the period. The largest contributors to the increase were side airbags and center airbags, followed by driver airbags, partly offset by declines for passenger airbags, steering wheels and inflatable curtains</font><font style="color:#ff0000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">.</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:12pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Sales by product &#x2013; Seatbelt Products and Other</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:12pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Sales for Seatbelt Products and Other declined organically* by 2.0% in the period. Sales decreased organically in Americas, China and EMEA while they increased in Asia excluding China.</font></p></td>
     </tr>
    </table><h2 style="tab-size:26.66px;padding-bottom:1pt;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #005496;text-align:justify;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"></font>&#160;</h2>
    <table style="margin-left:auto;border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:100.0%;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;">
     <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
      <td style="width:49%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:2%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:49%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
     </tr>
     <tr style="height:12pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:12pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Sales by region</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Our global organic sales* increased by 0.2% compared to the global LVP decrease of 0.9% (according to Mobility Global, Oct 2026). The relative outperformance was mainly driven by new product launches. Our organic sales growth outperformed LVP growth by 6.9pp in China and by 4.3pp in Asia excluding China. We underperformed LVP in EMEA by 3.7pp and by 3.5pp in Americas, impacted mainly by negative mix due to high LVP growth in lower content South America and a lower content on some replacement models.</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">LVP in China declined by 6.3%, with Global OEMs LVP declining by 16% and Chinese OEMs LVP decreased by 1.6%. Autoliv's sales to domestic OEMs increased organically by around 31% while our sales to global OEMs decreased by around 21%. Chinese OEMs accounted for 53% of our sales in China in the first nine months of 2026, compared to 41% a year ago. Our strong sales growth in Asia excluding China was mainly due to 34% organic sales growth in India, reflecting strong LVP growth but mainly the trend of increased safety content in vehicles in India.</font></p></td>
     </tr>
    </table><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p>
