    </table><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:8pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:8pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p>
    <table style="margin-left:auto;border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:100.0%;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;">
     <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
      <td style="width:50%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:1%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:49%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
     </tr>
     <tr style="height:14pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:14pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Third quarter 2026 development</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross profit</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $26 million, and gross margin decreased by 0.9pp compared to the prior year. The decrease in gross profit was mainly attributable to the $13 million gross profit impact of the supplier settlement compensation reported in Q3 2025, lower net sales and higher logistics costs.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">S,G&amp;A</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;costs increased by $1 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to slightly higher IT expenses and professional services costs partly offset by slightly lower personnel costs. S,G&amp;A costs in relation to sales were unchanged at 5.1%.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">R,D&amp;E, net,</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;costs decreased by $18 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to $26 million of higher engineering income related to timing effects, partly offset by adverse effects from FX translation, IT expenses and personnel costs. R,D&amp;E, net, in relation to sales decreased from 4.3% to 3.7%.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Other income (expense), net, </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">was negative $5 million, compared to negative $1 million in the same period last year. The negative $5 million in Q3 2026 consisted mainly of capacity alignment costs related to our restructuring activities in T&uuml;rkiye.</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating income</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $13 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to lower gross profit and higher capacity alignment costs, partly offset by lower R,D&amp;E, net, costs, as outlined above.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Adjusted operating income* </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">decreased by $9 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to the lower gross profit, partly offset by lower R,D&amp;E, net, costs, as outlined above.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Financial and non-operating items, net,</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;was a negative $24 million compared to a negative $27 million a year earlier. The improvement was mainly due to lower costs for non-operating items mainly related to positive FX effects.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Income before taxes</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $10 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to lower operating income, partly offset by lower costs for financial and non-operating items, net, as outlined above.</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Tax rate</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;was 32.5% compared to 26.9% in the prior year. Discrete tax items, net, had an unfavorable impact of 4.9pp in Q3 2026, while discrete tax items, net, had a favorable impact of 1.3pp in Q3 2025. Discrete tax items recorded in Q3 2026 primarily related to negative tax impacts from the closure of tax audits during the quarter.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Earnings per share, diluted</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $0.15 compared to the prior year. The main drivers were negative impacts of $0.16 from higher taxes and $0.13 from lower operating income partly offset by $0.11 from a lower number of outstanding shares, diluted and $0.05 from lower financial and non-operating items.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
     </tr>
    </table><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></div></div>
  <div class="fixed-width-container" style="margin-left:auto;padding-left:0.3in;width:7.67in;margin-top:auto;box-sizing:content-box;margin-right:auto;padding-right:0.3in;"><div style="z-index:2;flex-direction:column;display:flex;padding-bottom:0.3in;justify-content:flex-end;position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:11pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:right;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:11pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">7</font></p></div></div>
  <hr style="margin-inline-start:auto;margin-inline-end:auto;width:8.27in;page-break-after:always;">
  <div class="fixed-width-container" style="margin-left:auto;padding-left:0.3in;width:7.67in;box-sizing:content-box;margin-right:auto;padding-right:0.3in;"><div style="padding-top:0.4in;z-index:2;position:relative;box-sizing:border-box;">
    <table style="border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:100.0%;border-collapse:separate;">
     <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
      <td style="width:100%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
     </tr>
     <tr style="height:10pt;background-color:#0042a5;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;text-indent:7.2pt;padding-left:0.01in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0.01in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="margin-left:7.2pt;text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10.5pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left; margin-right:0;"><font style="color:#ffffff;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Financial Report July - September 2026</font></p></td>
     </tr>
    </table><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;margin-left:0;margin-right:0;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></div></div>
  <div class="main-content-container" style="z-index:5;position:relative;"><div class="fixed-width-container" style="margin-left:auto;padding-left:0.3in;width:7.67in;box-sizing:content-box;margin-right:auto;padding-right:0.3in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p>
    <table style="margin-left:auto;border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:100.0%;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;">
     <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
      <td style="width:50%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:1%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:49%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
     </tr>
     <tr style="height:14pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:14pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">First nine months 2026 development</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Gross profit</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;increased by $30 million while gross margin decreased by 0.2pp compared to the prior year. The drivers behind the gross profit improvement were mainly positive effects of higher sales and positive FX translation effects. This was partly offset by $25 million impact from a supplier compensation booked in Q3 2025 which was reversed in Q2 2026, and asset impairment related to the restructuring activities in T&uuml;rkiye.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">S,G&amp;A</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;costs increased by $10 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to negative FX translation effects and higher personnel costs, partly offset by the revision of an estimated credit loss reserve. S,G&amp;A costs in relation to sales were unchanged at 5.3%.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">R,D&amp;E, net,</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;costs increased by $22 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to higher personnel costs and negative FX translation effects, partly offset by higher engineering income. R,D&amp;E, net, in relation to sales increased from 4.0% to 4.1%.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Other income (expense), net, </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">was negative $70 million, compared to positive $13 million in the same period last year. The increase in costs was mainly due to higher capacity alignment costs related to restructuring activities in T&uuml;rkiye.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating income</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $86 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to higher capacity alignment costs related to restructuring activities in T&uuml;rkiye, higher R,D&amp;E, net, costs and higher S,G&amp;A costs, partly offset by higher gross profit as outlined above.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Adjusted operating income* </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">decreased by $1 million compared to the prior year, due to the higher costs for R,D&amp;E, net and S,G&amp;A offset by the higher gross profit, as outlined above.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Financial and non-operating items, net,</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;was negative $97 million compared to negative $76 million a year earlier. The increase in costs was mainly due to higher non-operating items, mainly related to costs associated with restructuring activities in T&uuml;rkiye and Mexico.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Income before taxes</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $107 million compared to the prior year, mainly due to lower operating income and higher costs for financial and non-operating items, net, as outlined above.</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Tax rate</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;was 32.2% compared to 26.4% in the prior year. Discrete tax items, net, for the period had an unfavorable impact of 4.2pp. Discrete tax items, net, for the prior year period had a favorable impact of 1.8pp. Discrete tax items recorded in the first nine months of 2026 primarily related to negative tax impacts from closure of tax audits during the third quarter and negative tax impacts recorded in the first half year from costs recorded for the capacity alignment activities for Autoliv&#x2019;s manufacturing operations in T&uuml;rkiye.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Earnings per share, diluted</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $1.23 compared to the prior year. The main drivers were negative impacts of $0.82 from lower operating income, $0.43 from higher tax and $0.18 from financial and non-operating items, partly offset by $0.22 from a lower number of outstanding shares, diluted.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
     </tr>
