     <tr style="height:7pt;background-color:#ffffff;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td colspan="4" style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:middle;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:7pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">1) </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Outstanding receivables and outstanding inventory less outstanding payables. Non-GAAP measure, see reconciliation table. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">2)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Outstanding receivables and outstanding inventory less outstanding payables relative to annualized quarterly sales. Non-GAAP measure, see reconciliation table. Annualized quarterly sales is calculated as the quarterly sales amount multiplied by four. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">3)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Outstanding receivables relative to annualized quarterly sales. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">4)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Outstanding inventory relative to annualized quarterly sales. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">5)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Outstanding payables relative to annualized quarterly sales. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">6)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Short- and long-term interest-bearing debt. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">7)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Short- and long-term debt less cash and cash equivalents and debt-related derivatives. Non-GAAP measure. See reconciliation table. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">8)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Total equity and net debt. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">9)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Annualized operating income and income from equity method investments, relative to average capital employed. See definitions of &#34;Annualized operating income&#34; in footnote to the reconciliation tables below. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">10)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Annualized net income relative to average total equity. See definitions of &#34;Annualized net income&#34; in footnote to the reconciliation tables below. </font><font style="color:#000000;top:-3.283pt;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:4.69pt;line-height:1.5;position:relative;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">11)</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;Net debt adjusted for pension liabilities in relation to EBITDA. Non-GAAP measure. See reconciliation table.</font></p></td>
     </tr>
    </table><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p>
    <table style="margin-left:auto;border-spacing:0;table-layout:auto;width:100.0%;border-collapse:separate;margin-right:auto;">
     <tr style="visibility:collapse;">
      <td style="width:49%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:2%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
      <td style="width:49%;box-sizing:content-box;"></td>
     </tr>
     <tr style="height:14pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:14pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#0042a5;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Third quarter 2026 development</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Changes in operating working capital </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">had a $45 million negative impact on operating cash flow compared to a negative impact of $53 million in the prior year. The $45 million increase in operating working capital resulted mainly from $71 million in higher inventories and $21 million from receivables, net, partly offset by $52 million from accounts payable and accrued liabilities.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Operating cash flow</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;decreased by $19 million to $239 million compared to the prior year, mainly because of lower net income, partly offset by a smaller increase in operating working capital compared to last year.</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:14pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Capital expenditure, net, </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">increased by $9 million compared to the prior year. The level of capital expenditure, net, in relation to sales increased to 4.3% versus 3.9% a year earlier.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Free operating cash flow*</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;was positive $124 million compared to positive $153 million in the prior year. The decrease was due to lower operating cash flow and higher capital expenditure, net, as outlined above.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Cash conversion*</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;defined as free operating cash flow* in relation to net income, was 80% compared to 87% a year earlier.</font></p></td>
     </tr>
