     <tr style="height:10pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Trade working capital* </font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">in relation to sales decreased from 13.9% to 13.5%. The improvement was mainly driven by higher payables in relation to sales while inventories and receivables to sales were relatively unchanged.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-weight:bold;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Net debt*</font><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;was $1,763 million as of September 30, 2026, which was $9 million lower than a year earlier.</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:6pt;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
