     <tr style="height:10pt;word-break:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap;text-align:left;">
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;text-indent:12.95pt;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;margin-left:0.0201388888888889in;text-indent:0;tab-size:32px;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:6pt;min-width:0.1597222222222222in;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.272902758787099%;word-break:keep-all;text-indent:0;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">On September 8, 2026, Autoliv announced it is advancing the development of virtual testing through its Human Body Model (HBM) Safety Suite. The platform is designed to support the development of safer vehicles, with Toyota as the first customer to evaluate its capabilities. </font></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;margin-left:0.0201388888888889in;text-indent:0;tab-size:32px;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:6pt;min-width:0.1597222222222222in;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.272902758787099%;word-break:keep-all;text-indent:0;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">On October 2, 2026, Autoliv announced the appointments of Natalie Draisin and Thomas Manfred </font><font style="color:#212529;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">M&uuml;ller to its Research Advisory Board. Natalie Draisin serves as Director of the North American Office and United Nations Representative at FIA Foundation and is an External Affiliate at Johns Hopkins Bloomberg School of Public Health. Thomas Manfred M&uuml;ller, PhD, is a Board Member, Advisor and Business Angel with extensive international experience across leadership and executive roles at Audi, BMW, Volvo Cars, and Volkswagen Group.</font></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;margin-left:0.0201388888888889in;text-indent:0;tab-size:32px;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:0;min-width:0.1597222222222222in;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.272902758787099%;word-break:keep-all;text-indent:0;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Autoliv today published on its website its Green Financing Framework which has been updated to incorporate the latest market practices and standards, and to support the long-term commitment of the Company to integrate sustainability across the entire organization.</font></div></div><p style="text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><p style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
      <td style="padding-top:0.01in;text-indent:12.95pt;padding-left:0in;vertical-align:top;padding-bottom:0in;padding-right:0.01in;"><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;margin-left:0.0201388888888889in;text-indent:0;tab-size:32px;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:6pt;min-width:0.1597222222222222in;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.272902758787099%;word-break:keep-all;text-indent:0;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">In Q3 2026, Autoliv repurchased and retired 1.23 million shares of common stock at an average price of $121.69 per share under the Autoliv 2029 stock repurchase program. Under this program, repurchases may be made from July 1, 2025 through December 31, 2029. The maximum value of aggregate repurchases under this program is $2.5 billion. Repurchases of stock may be made directly on the NYSE.</font></div></div><div class="item-list-element-wrapper" style="display:flex;font-size:10pt;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;margin-left:0.0201388888888889in;text-indent:0;tab-size:32px;margin-top:0;justify-content:flex-start;font-family:Arial;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:6pt;min-width:0.1597222222222222in;text-align:left;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:Times New Roman;font-kerning:none;min-width:4.272902758787099%;word-break:keep-all;text-indent:0;display:inline-flex;justify-content:flex-start;">&#x2022;</font><div style="display:inline;"><font style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Autoliv invites investors, analysts and journalists to an Investor Day in Shanghai, China. It will take place on April 26 and 27, 2027, with management presentations, site visits and a full day at the world's leading auto show, Auto Shanghai 2027. Focus will be on global growth, innovations and key trends shaping China&#x2019;s automotive industry and Autoliv&#x2019;s strategy for success in the Chinese market. This includes how we strengthen our relationships with leading Chinese OEMs in China and overseas. Further details regarding agenda and registration will be provided at a later stage.</font></div></div><p style="text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p><p style="text-indent:0;tab-size:26.66px;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:6pt;margin-right:0.0798611111111111in;text-align:left;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</font></p></td>
     </tr>
    </table><h2 style="tab-size:26.66px;padding-bottom:1pt;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #005496;text-align:justify;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"></font>&#160;</h2><h2 style="tab-size:26.66px;font-size:9pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Arial;margin-bottom:0;text-align:justify;"><font style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:9pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"></font>&#160;</h2>
